 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "How the falling leaves fall on above,\nThe life that hath passed away away;\nThe woman who alone\nLay sheltered in her maidenhood's day,\nIn the lone, lonely world of beauty;\nBut now that time has ceased to hesitate,\nShe bends at last down to forgive\nHer lost and ruined lover--her great,\nMighty one; but with an silent\nPains and tears she sighs separated.\nO children! O sons, forget!\nForget once more all that always",
